After <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-features-to-try-first/">releasing iOS 27</a> last week, Apple is already testing a follow-up iOS 27.0.1 update for iPhones, according to <em>MacRumors</em> logs.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27-0-1.jpeg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067074" /><br/>
iOS 27.0.1 will likely be a minor update with bug fixes and/or security patches.<br/>
<br/>
Shortly after Apple launches new iPhone models, some software bugs are usually discovered as the devices get into the hands of millions of customers around the world. This year, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/iphone-18-pro-face-id-issues/">some iPhone 18 Pro users are experiencing Face ID issues</a>, so it is likely that iOS 27.0.1 will include some Face ID-related bug fixes or enhancements at a minimum.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/23/watchos-27-0-1-release/">watchOS 27.0.1 is already available</a> for the Apple Watch Series 12 and Apple Watch Ultra 4. That update fixes an issue where those models may restart unexpectedly.<br/>
